# Python bytecode caches (from running scripts/build_lot2_5_spec.py etc.)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# A local Spark session writes its warehouse to the working directory unless
# told otherwise, so running the emitted chain against a real Spark leaves this
# beside the deliveries. It is not one of them.
#
# This keeps it out of a commit and nothing more. It is not a guard for
# validation/hygiene/study_folder_standalone.R, which reads the filesystem and
# never consults this file: that suite counts every sibling directory and fails
# when a Jul 28 file names one. It stays green on this directory only because
# no file says "spark-warehouse" - a scratch directory called something a
# delivery file does mention would still fail it, which is how an empty
# artifacts/ broke the gate once.
spark-warehouse/

# Every package writes its run outputs to its own out/. They are generated, and
# the documented preview commands - the scenario workbook, the audit counts, the
# QC report - write them without a warehouse, so running what the runbook says
# would otherwise leave the tree dirty and a handover unclear about what changed.
#
# The catalogues that ARE deliverables (the rule vignettes, the definition
# concordance) are already tracked, and git does not stop following a file it is
# already following - so this hides new generated output only.
out/
